      "hints": [
        "Set $\\frac{dy}{dx} = 0 \\implies (2x - 7)^2 = 9 \\implies 2x - 7 = \\pm 3$.",
        "Solve for $x = 5$ and $x = 2$, then calculate the corresponding $y$-coordinates."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Set the first derivative equal to zero to locate the stationary points:\n$$54 - 6(2x - 7)^2 = 0 \\implies 6(2x - 7)^2 = 54 \\implies (2x - 7)^2 = 9$$",
        "Take square roots:\n$$2x - 7 = 3 \\implies 2x = 10 \\implies x = 5$$\n$$2x - 7 = -3 \\implies 2x = 4 \\implies x = 2$$",
        "Evaluate the $y$-coordinates using $y = 54x - (2x - 7)^3$:\n$$\\text{For } x = 5: \\quad y = 54(5) - (10 - 7)^3 = 270 - 27 = 243 \\implies (5, 243)$$\n$$\\text{For } x = 2: \\quad y = 54(2) - (4 - 7)^3 = 108 - (-27) = 135 \\implies (2, 135)$$"
      ],
